  model:"Customer is a 46-year-old garment retailer, a nine-year relationship rated Low risk, with a savings account profiled for household use at INR 40,000–80,000 monthly. Alert NT-006 triggered on a collection-and-payout pattern matching the institution's funnel-account profile: 19–22 credits of INR 10,000 per month from a stable group, one outbound lump sum of approximately INR 2,00,000 per month, cash deposits present, retention near zero.\n\nThe surface pattern is a genuine match to the funnel typology and was investigated on that basis. Three lines of analysis resolved it. First, the review window was extended to 26 months: the pattern is unbroken from June 2023, and across that period 21 distinct individuals have each received exactly one payout in a fixed sequence, after which the cycle restarted. Second, reciprocity analysis established that all 21 counterparties both contribute and receive, that recipients continue contributing after their payout, and that there are no one-way payers and no recipients who never pay. Third, value reconciliation shows aggregate contributions of approximately INR 2,10,000 per month against payouts of approximately INR 2,06,000, matching to within 1.9% over 26 months, with no accumulation and nothing paid to any party outside the group.\n\nThe customer produced a handwritten committee register covering the full period: the 21-member list, monthly contribution entries, the payout order agreed at the outset, the recipient and date each month, and a signed acknowledgement from each recipient. Entries reconcile line by line to the account. The register discloses an organiser's fee of INR 1,000 per month, which matches the residual retention exactly. Cash deposits totalling INR 5.2 lakh across 26 months, roughly 9% of contributions, were made by the customer herself at her local branch, confirmed on CCTV, in amounts corresponding to the contributors recorded as paying in cash. Seventeen of the 21 counterparties are identifiable in the same market district, nine as proprietors of neighbouring businesses. Screening returned no matches for the customer or any counterparty.\n\nThe funnel typology requires value to move one way through an account keeper to beneficiaries who never contribute. That condition does not hold. Source of funds is established as member contributions, corroborated by the register, the acknowledgements, the reciprocity analysis and 26 months of consistent behaviour; the customer's own business income is a separate flow in a separate account, evidenced by GST returns.\n\nThe activity is unusual for a savings account declared for household use and should never have been left unexamined, but it is reasonably explained and no money laundering typology is indicated. Recommendation: close with no suspicion. Record two residual actions: first, update the KYC profile to reflect the rotating savings activity, its expected monthly value and the counterparty group, so comparable activity is triaged correctly; second, refer to the business the question of whether a personal savings account is the appropriate product and whether the arrangement engages chit fund licensing requirements — a conduct and product matter, not an anti-money-laundering suspicion. Note for control purposes that the January 2024 alert on identical activity was closed without obtaining any documents, which left the risk untested for 19 months."
